      "id": "alg-adaptive-truncated-covariance-estimator",
      "location": "Definition",
      "defect": "ill-formed",
      "evidence": "The Definition says “Partition the indices deterministically into k nonempty blocks whose sizes differ by at most one,” but does not specify which partition. The dependency alg-geometric-median-of-block-means separately says “Form consecutive blocks ... in index order,” and this Definition does not say to use that rule here. For β=1.1, k=4, m=8 and scalar sample (0,0,0,0,100,100,100,100), consecutive pairs give block means (0,0,100,100) and minimum-norm geometric median 0; deterministic alternating pairs (i,i+4) give four means of 50 and pilot 50. Both partitions meet the stated size condition, so the procedure does not specify a unique output.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
